      "title": "RTP: Have dynamic payload type show up as new Decode As item",
      "message": "RTP: Have dynamic payload type show up as new Decode As item\n\nThe Decode As dialog, when adding a new item, auto-populates\nwith the data from the last Decode As item to appear in the frame.\nThis is because usually the presence of a Decode As item indicates\nthat previous protocols were dissected correctly.\n\nThe RTP protocol obscures the dynamic payload types because they\nweren't presented in the prompt for the old GTK+ Decode As widget.\nThe prompts aren't used at all in Qt, but obscuring the dynamic\npayload type means that the Decode As model and delegate don't\npresent dynamic payload types as something that can be changed in\nthe current packet.\n\nChange that, so if you select Decode As on a packet that has, e.g.\nRTP over UDP, it will prefer changing the RTP payload type dissector\nto changing the dissector for the UDP port.\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
